# frozen file stop it before any assertion about the implementation is evaluated.
#
#   1. scripts/checks/S18.sh:19 - target_defined() is
#        make -pRrq : 2>/dev/null | grep -Eq "^$1:( |$)"
#      `make -pRrq :` exits 2 ("No rule to make target `:'") and a Makefile cannot define a
#      target named `:` - a bare `:` line is make's empty rule, not that target. When grep -q
#      matches it closes the pipe early, and make dies of SIGPIPE (141). The script runs under
#      `set -o pipefail`, so the pipeline is non-zero either way and target_defined() is false
#      even for a target that is defined: `FAIL: no make target 'demo-up'`. Without pipefail
#      the same pipeline returns 0.
#
#   2. scripts/checks/S18.sh:40 - `python3 - <<'PY' <<<"$state"`
#      The herestring is applied after the heredoc, so the JSON replaces the script on fd 0 and
#      python executes the read model as its own source: NameError: name 'true' is not defined.
#
# This log is that same file with those two mechanics corrected in a throwaway copy
# (scripts/checks/S18-probe.sh: the make pipeline grouped with `|| true` before grep, and the
# read model passed as argv instead of as stdin). No assertion was changed, weakened or added.
# The gate itself stays frozen for the human to rule on - see the session report.
